# THE SECOND CAUSE: FACES FOUND, NONE CONFIRMED.
#
# Recognition ran and has 63 proposals waiting. The list is empty because a
# proposal is not a photograph of someone until a member has said so — which is
# the same law `PersonRow.photo_count` keeps ("confirmed regions only") read
# from the other end.
#
# This fixture and `photos-people/recognition-off` are byte-different in exactly
# the two fields that matter, and a screen that only checked `people.isEmpty()`
# would draw them identically. The answer here is a DOOR — review, with its
# count on it — and the answer there is a setting. Offering review on a vault
# with recognition off would open an empty queue; offering a setting to a member
# with 63 questions waiting would hide the work.
#
# `EMPTY_REASON_NOT_RUN_YET`, the third cause, is the one v0's single sentence
# fit least badly, and it is why the enum has three values and not a bool.
seat {
  availability: AVAILABILITY_READY
  durability: DURABILITY_AUTHORITATIVE
  connectivity: CONNECTIVITY_ONLINE_UNMETERED
}
data {
  proposed_face_count: 63
  empty_reason: EMPTY_REASON_NONE_NAMED
}
